<title>USA: Italy's Dini sees no problem with convergence plan.</title>
<headline>Italy's Dini sees no problem with convergence plan.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-06-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian Foreign Minister Lamberto Dini said on Saturday he did not foresee any problems arising from Italy's economic convergence plan which is to be examined by the EU's influential monetary committee next week.</p>
<p>&quot;I do not expect any problems, Italy is doing very well in this regard,&quot; said Dini.</p>
<p>Italy has submitted to the European Union's executive commission a plan for economic convergence with other EU member countries in advance of joining a planned currency union.</p>
<p>The monetary committee is to look at the plan at a meeting on June 25 and it will then be submitted to EU Finance Ministers for approval on July 7.</p>
</text>
